%U A398648 5467447,6064687,6299047,6453847,7395247,7578127,7938487,8115967,8396191,8568991,9076591,9503407,9664327,9823447,9949447,9980767
%N A398648 Numbers k such that psi(k) = phi(k) + tau(k)^7.
%C A398648 Contains all numbers of the form p*(2^13-p), where p and 2^13-p are both prime. Are there any other terms that are not of this form?
%e A398648 106327 is a term since psi(106327) = 114520 = 98136 + 4^7 = phi(106327) + tau(106327)^7.
%o A398648 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) - eulerphi(f) == numdiv(f)^7; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 09 2026
